From 229e33d9b7c9c3c0876be8446a3f9499f8723316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elpaablo <donopwhile1@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 02:14:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] art: drop non-AOSP global -O3
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Revert of 93f3df814f ("art: Optimize the entirity of ART for
performance"). Global -O3 on ART is an unbenchmarked, non-AOSP perf
flag on an unusually UB-sensitive codebase (Unsafe/reflection
field-offset bridges, memory-order-sensitive runtime internals), where
wrong-code manifests as silent bad data rather than crashes. ART's hot
paths (assembly stubs, JIT output, dexpreopted oat) don't get faster
from -O3 in libart's C++, so the upside is ~zero and the risk is
asymmetric. Stay on AOSP-default optimization flags.

Historical note: this originally landed as a test while investigating
the OplusCamera protobuf feature-table empty-parse (modeTableSize 0)
on astonc. That issue was later attributed to a camera userspace/config
mismatch (fixed by the GLOBAL 12R_400 userspace swap in
vendor/oplus/camera), not to -O3 — the revert is kept on its own
merits above.
---
 build/Android.bp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/Android.bp b/build/Android.bp
index 20a851d..7feb8fc 100644
--- a/build/Android.bp
+++ b/build/Android.bp
@@ -108,7 +108,6 @@ art_global_defaults {
         "-Wshadow",
         "-Wunused",
         "-fvisibility=protected",
-        "-O3",
 
         // Warn about thread safety violations with clang.
         "-Wthread-safety",
-- 
2.43.0

